%% Glacier logic - from 77act1.mud GLACIER and GLACIER-ROOM routines

~(glacier-flag)

%% ICY
#glacier-room
(room *)
(name *)	Glacier Room
(inherently dark *)
(look *)
	You are in a large room, with giant icicles hanging from the walls
	and ceiling.  There are passages to the north and east.
	(if) (glacier-flag) (then) There is a large passageway leading westward. (endif)
(from * go #north to #stream)
(from * go #east to #egyptian-room)
(from * go #west to #ruby-room)
(prevent [from * go #west])
	~(glacier-flag)
    You can't go that way.

%% ICE
#glacier
(* is #in #glacier-room)
(name *)	glacier
(dict *)	ice
(appearance *)
	A mass of ice fills the western half of the room.

%% Object action: GLACIER - throw torch at glacier to melt it

(grammar [melt [object]] for [melt $])
(grammar [melt [object] with [object]] for [melt $ with $])

(perform [melt $obj])
    How exactly are you going to melt (the $obj)?
    (tick) (stop)

(perform [melt $ with $])
    That doesn't seem to work.

%% THROW TORCH AT GLACIER

(perform [throw #torch at #glacier])
    The torch hits the glacier and explodes into a great ball of flame,
    devouring the glacier.  The water from the melting glacier rushes
    downstream, carrying the torch with it.  In the place of the glacier,
    there is a passageway leading west.
    (now) (#torch is #in #stream)
    (now) (#glacier is nowhere)
    (now) (glacier-flag)
    (if) ~(room is lit) (then)
        (par)
        The melting glacier seems to have carried the torch away, leaving
        you in the dark.
    (endif)
    (tick) (stop)

%% Generic throw at glacier rejection
(perform [throw $ at #glacier])
    The glacier is unmoved by your ridiculous attempt.
    (tick) (stop)
